# English editions, batch 2 — original English meanings by OmKiran Bhakti.
from en_texts import EN

EN["durga-chalisa.html"] = dict(
 name="Durga Chalisa", sub="40 chaupais, with English meaning",
 title="Durga Chalisa — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Full Shri Durga Chalisa (Namo Namo Durge Sukh Karni) lyrics in English (Roman) and Hindi, with a simple English meaning of every chaupai. For Navratri, Ashtami and Fridays.",
 answer="The Shri Durga Chalisa, beginning 'Namo Namo Durge Sukh Karni', was written by the poet Devidas. Its forty chaupais describe the many forms of Maa Durga and her victories over the demons. Each verse below is in English letters, in Devanagari, and explained in plain English.",
 intro="It is recited on all nine days of Navratri, on Ashtami and every Friday, with a lamp lit in the morning or evening puja.",
 author="Devidas",
 m=["Salutations to Durga, giver of happiness; salutations to Mother Ambe, remover of sorrow.",
 "Your light is formless, and its radiance spreads through all three worlds.",
 "The moon rests on your forehead, your face is vast, your eyes are red and your brows fierce.",
 "The Mother's form is supremely beautiful; devotees feel great joy at her darshan.",
 "All the power of the universe rests in you, and you give food and wealth to sustain it.",
 "As Annapurna you nourish the world; you are also the primordial beautiful maiden.",
 "At the time of dissolution you destroy everything, and you are Gauri, beloved of Shiva.",
 "Shiva and the yogis sing your virtues; Brahma and Vishnu meditate on you every day.",
 "Taking the form of Saraswati you gave good sense to the sages and uplifted them.",
 "O Amba, it was you who took the form of Narasimha and burst out of the pillar.",
 "You protected and saved Prahlad and sent the demon to heaven by granting him liberation.",
 "In the world you took the form of Lakshmi and dwell with Shri Narayan.",
 "You live in the ocean of milk; O ocean of compassion, fulfil the hopes of my heart.",
 "At Hinglaj you are Bhavani; your boundless glory cannot be described.",
 "Matangi, Dhumavati, Bhuvaneshwari and Bagalamukhi, givers of happiness — all of them are you.",
 "As Bhairavi, as Tara who carries the world across, and as Chhinnamasta, you remove the sorrows of worldly life.",
 "Bhavani shines riding the lion, and the brave Langur (Hanuman) walks ahead of her.",
 "In your hands are the skull-bowl and the sword; at the sight of them even death runs in fear.",
 "Your weapons and trident gleam, striking fear into the hearts of enemies.",
 "You reside at Nagarkot (Kangra), and your drum of victory sounds through the three worlds.",
 "You killed the demons Shumbh and Nishumbh and destroyed countless demons like Raktabeej.",
 "The demon king Mahishasur was very arrogant; the earth groaned under the weight of his sins.",
 "Taking the terrible form of Kali, you destroyed him along with his army.",
 "Whenever the saints faced hardship, Mother, you came to their aid.",
 "The city of the gods and Indra's realm stay free of sorrow only by your glory.",
 "Your flame burns at Jwala Devi, and men and women worship you always.",
 "Sorrow and poverty never come near those who sing your glory with love and devotion.",
 "Whoever meditates on you with a focused mind is freed from the cycle of birth and death.",
 "Yogis, gods and sages proclaim that yoga is impossible without your power.",
 "The teacher Shankar performed austerities and conquered desire and anger.",
 "Day and night he meditated on Shiva, but never once remembered you.",
 "He did not grasp the secret of Shakti; when his power left him, he regretted it.",
 "Then he took refuge in you and sang your glory: victory, victory, victory to Jagadamba Bhavani!",
 "The primordial Mother was pleased and returned his power without delay.",
 "Mother, great troubles surround me; who but you can take away my sorrow?",
 "Hopes and cravings torment me; destroy my attachment, pride and all such faults.",
 "O great Queen, destroy my enemies; O Bhavani, I remember you with a single-pointed mind.",
 "Be gracious, kind Mother, and bless me with prosperity and success.",
 "As long as I live may I receive your mercy, and may I always tell of your glory.",
 "Whoever sings the Shri Durga Chalisa enjoys every happiness and reaches the highest state.",
 "Knowing Devidas to be in your refuge, O Jagadamba Bhavani, be gracious to him.",
 "The Mother protects those who take refuge in her, so her devotee lives without fear. Mother, I have come to your refuge — take me into your lap."],
 faqs=[("Who wrote the Durga Chalisa?","By tradition it is the work of Devidas, whose name appears in the last chaupai."),
       ("When should the Durga Chalisa be recited?","On the nine days of Navratri, on Ashtami and every Friday, with a lamp lit during the morning or evening puja.")])

EN["shiv-chalisa.html"] = dict(
 name="Shiv Chalisa", sub="40 chaupais, with English meaning",
 title="Shiv Chalisa — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Full Shiv Chalisa (Jai Girija Pati Deen Dayala) lyrics in English (Roman) and Hindi, with a simple English meaning of every verse. For Mondays, Pradosh, Sawan and Mahashivratri.",
 answer="The Shiv Chalisa, beginning 'Jai Girija Pati Deen Dayala', was written by Ayodhyadas. It describes Lord Shiva's form, his great deeds and his grace towards devotees. Each verse below is in English letters, in Devanagari, and explained in plain English.",
 intro="Mondays, Pradosh (trayodashi), the month of Sawan and Mahashivratri are especially auspicious for it, and it can be read every morning.",
 author="Ayodhyadas",
 m=["Victory to Ganesh, son of Girija, root of all that is auspicious and full of wisdom. Says Ayodhyadas: grant me the boon of fearlessness.",
 "Victory to you, husband of Parvati, merciful to the humble; you always protect the saints.",
 "The moon shines beautifully on your forehead, and your earrings are shaped like serpent hoods.",
 "Your body is fair, the Ganga flows from your head, you wear a garland of skulls and your body is smeared with ash.",
 "A tiger skin is your garment; even serpents are charmed by your appearance.",
 "Parvati, the beloved daughter of Mother Maina, shines at your left side with a unique beauty.",
 "The trident in your hand looks mighty and always destroys your enemies.",
 "Nandi and Ganesh look there like lotuses in the middle of the ocean.",
 "With Kartikeya and Ganapati beside you, no one can describe this sight.",
 "Whenever the gods called out to you, Lord, you removed their sorrow at once.",
 "When the demon Tarak caused great havoc, all the gods together pleaded with you.",
 "You sent six-faced Kartikeya at once, who struck him down in the blink of an eye.",
 "You destroyed the demon Jalandhar; your glory is known throughout the world.",
 "You fought the demon Tripurasur and, in your mercy, saved everyone.",
 "Bhagirath performed great austerities, and you, destroyer of Tripura, fulfilled his vow by holding the Ganga.",
 "Among givers there is none like you; your servants praise you always.",
 "The Vedas sang the glory of your name, yet none could fathom your indescribable, beginningless mystery.",
 "When the ocean was churned, a blaze of poison rose up and the gods and demons burned in distress.",
 "Then in your mercy you drank it and helped them all, and so you came to be called Neelkanth, the blue-throated.",
 "Shri Ram worshipped you, conquered Lanka and gave the kingdom to Vibhishan.",
 "When Shri Ram was worshipping you with a thousand lotuses, you tested him.",
 "You hid one lotus, so the lotus-eyed Ram set out to offer his own eye in its place.",
 "Seeing such intense devotion, Lord Shankar was pleased and granted the boon he wished.",
 "Victory, victory, victory to the infinite, the imperishable, who lives in every heart and is gracious to all.",
 "All the wicked trouble me every day; I wander about and find no peace.",
 "O Lord, I cry out 'save me, save me' — come now and rescue me.",
 "Take up your trident, strike down my enemies and rescue me from danger.",
 "Mother, father, brothers — everyone is there, yet in trouble no one asks after you.",
 "Master, you alone are my hope; come and remove my heavy troubles.",
 "You always give wealth to the poor; whoever asks of you receives the reward.",
 "How can we possibly praise you? Forgive our mistakes, O Lord.",
 "O Shankar, you destroy troubles, bring auspiciousness and remove obstacles.",
 "Yogis, ascetics and sages meditate on you; Saraswati and Narad bow their heads to you.",
 "Salutations, salutations, victory — Namah Shivaya! Even the gods and Brahma cannot reach your limit.",
 "Whoever recites this with full attention, Shambhu comes to their aid.",
 "Anyone burdened with debt who recites this is freed from it.",
 "Whoever longs for a child surely receives Shiva's grace.",
 "On trayodashi, invite a priest and have a havan performed with devotion.",
 "One who always keeps the trayodashi (Pradosh) fast has no suffering in the body.",
 "Offer incense, a lamp and food, and recite this before Shankar.",
 "The sins of many lifetimes are destroyed, and at the end one reaches Shiva's abode.",
 "Says Ayodhyadas: my hope is in you alone — knowing this, take away all my sorrows.",
 "Every morning, as a rule, I recite this chalisa; O Lord of the world, fulfil my heart's wish.",
 "In the month of Margashirsha, on the sixth day, in the Hemant season of Samvat sixty-four, this auspicious chalisa in praise of Shiva was completed."],
 faqs=[("Who wrote the Shiv Chalisa?","Ayodhyadas; his name appears in the first doha and in the last chaupai."),
       ("When should the Shiv Chalisa be recited?","On Mondays, on trayodashi (Pradosh), throughout Sawan and on Mahashivratri; it can also be read every morning.")])

EN["ganesh-chalisa.html"] = dict(
 name="Ganesh Chalisa", sub="With the story of Ganesh's birth",
 title="Ganesh Chalisa — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Full Shri Ganesh Chalisa (Jai Ganpati Sadgun Sadan) lyrics in English (Roman) and Hindi, with a simple English meaning of every verse, including the story of Ganesh's birth.",
 answer="The Ganesh Chalisa, beginning 'Jai Ganpati Sadgun Sadan', was written by Ramsundar. It tells how Ganesh was born, how he received an elephant's head and how he became the first to be worshipped. Each verse below is in English letters, in Devanagari, and explained in plain English.",
 intro="It is recited on Wednesdays, on Sankashti Chaturthi and during Ganesh Chaturthi.",
 author="Ramsundar",
 m=["Victory to Ganpati, home of all virtues, kind-hearted, remover of obstacles and bringer of good — victory to the son of Girija!",
 "Victory, victory to Ganpati, king of the ganas, who fills life with blessings and completes every good work.",
 "Victory to the elephant-faced one, giver of happiness, leader of the world and giver of intelligence.",
 "Your curved trunk is beautiful, and the three-line tilak on your forehead delights the heart.",
 "A garland of jewels and pearls shines on your chest; a golden crown is on your head and your eyes are large.",
 "In your hands are a book, an axe and a trident; you are offered modaks and fragrant flowers.",
 "Your body is adorned with beautiful yellow cloth, and your sandals dwell in the minds of the sages.",
 "Blessed is the son of Shiva, brother of Kartikeya, darling of Gauri, famous throughout the world.",
 "Riddhi and Siddhi wave the fly-whisk for you, and your mouse vehicle waits at the door.",
 "Now I tell the holy and auspicious story of your birth.",
 "Once Parvati, daughter of the king of mountains, performed great austerities for a son.",
 "When that matchless ritual was complete, you arrived in the form of a Brahmin.",
 "Seeing a guest, Gauri was happy and served you in many ways.",
 "Greatly pleased, you granted a boon, because the Mother had performed austerities for a son.",
 "'You will have a son of great intelligence, right now, without carrying him in your womb.'",
 "'He will lead the ganas, be a treasury of virtue and wisdom, be worshipped first, and be divine.'",
 "Saying this you vanished, and appeared in the cradle as a baby.",
 "When, as an infant, you began to cry, Gauri's joy at seeing your face knew no bounds.",
 "Everyone rejoiced and sang songs of blessing, and the gods showered flowers from the sky.",
 "Shiva and Uma gave away gifts generously; gods and sages came to see the son.",
 "Seeing such joy and celebration, Shani Dev too came to see the child.",
 "Thinking of the flaw in his own gaze, Shani did not want to look at the child.",
 "Girija felt hurt and asked: does my celebration not please you, Shani?",
 "Shani replied hesitantly: what will you gain by showing me the child?",
 "Uma did not believe him and asked Shani to look at the child.",
 "As soon as Shani's glance fell on him, the child's head flew off into the sky.",
 "Girija fell to the ground in anguish; that grief cannot be described.",
 "Kailash was filled with cries that Shani's gaze had destroyed the son.",
 "At once Vishnu rode out on Garuda, cut off an elephant's head with his discus and brought it back.",
 "He placed it on the child's body, and Shankar chanted a mantra and breathed life into it.",
 "Then Shambhu named him Ganesh and blessed him to be worshipped first and to be a treasury of wisdom.",
 "When Shiva tested their intelligence, he asked his sons to go around the earth.",
 "Six-faced Kartikeya set off on the journey, while you sat and thought of a wise solution.",
 "You held the feet of your mother and father and walked around them seven times.",
 "'Blessed is Ganesh!' said Shiva, delighted, and the gods showered many flowers from the sky.",
 "Even the thousand-mouthed serpent Shesh cannot sing the full glory of your wisdom.",
 "I am without wisdom, impure and sorrowful — how can I offer you my prayer?",
 "Ramsundar, the Lord's servant from Kakra-Durvasa near Prayag, sings your praise.",
 "O Lord, have mercy on this humble one now and give me some of your strength and devotion.",
 "Whoever recites this Shri Ganesh Chalisa with attention has new blessings in the home every day and is respected in the world.",
 "On the day of Rishi Panchami this chalisa of auspicious Ganesh was completed."],
 faqs=[("What story does the Ganesh Chalisa tell?","How Ganesh was born from Mother Parvati's austerities, lost his head to Shani's gaze, received an elephant's head, and became the first to be worshipped by circling his parents."),
       ("When is the Ganesh Chalisa recited?","On Wednesdays, on Sankashti Chaturthi and during the ten days of Ganesh Chaturthi.")])

EN["aarti-kunj-bihari-ki.html"] = dict(
 name="Aarti Kunj Bihari Ki", sub="Krishna aarti, with English meaning",
 title="Aarti Kunj Bihari Ki — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Aarti Kunj Bihari Ki (Shri Krishna aarti) lyrics in English letters and Hindi, with the meaning of every verse in simple English. Sung on Janmashtami, Ekadashi and in daily Krishna puja.",
 answer="'Aarti Kunj Bihari Ki' is the most popular aarti of Shri Krishna. It paints Vrindavan, the flute, the beauty of Radha and Krishna, and the Ganga flowing from Krishna's feet. The aarti is given below in English letters and Devanagari, with the meaning of each verse in English.",
 intro="It is sung on Janmashtami, on Ekadashi and in the evening aarti of daily Krishna worship.",
 m=["The aarti of Kunj Bihari — Krishna who roams the groves — Murari who lifted Govardhan.",
    "A vaijayanti garland at his neck, a sweet flute at his lips, earrings glinting in his ears — the darling of Nand. Dark as the sky, with radiant Radha beside him; curls like black bees, a musk tilak and a moon-like glow — the beautiful sight of Radha and Shyam.",
    "His golden peacock crown shines and the gods long for his darshan; flowers rain from the sky, the murchang and mridang play, and the gopis are lost in love.",
    "From his feet came forth the Ganga who captivates every heart and lives in Shiva's matted hair — such is the glory of Shri Banwari's feet.",
    "The sand of the Yamuna bank sparkles, the flute plays in Vrindavan, gopis, cowherds and cows are all around. His gentle smile and the moonlight cut the bonds of the world — O Lord, hear the cry of this humble one."],
 faqs=[("When is Aarti Kunj Bihari Ki sung?","On Janmashtami, on Ekadashi, and in the daily worship of Shri Krishna, especially at the evening aarti.")])

EN["hanuman-aarti.html"] = dict(
 name="Aarti Kije Hanuman Lala Ki", sub="Hanuman aarti, with English meaning",
 title="Aarti Kije Hanuman Lala Ki — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Aarti Kije Hanuman Lala Ki lyrics in English letters and Hindi with a simple English meaning of every verse. Sung after the Hanuman Chalisa on Tuesdays and Saturdays.",
 answer="'Aarti Kije Hanuman Lala Ki' is the most widely sung aarti of Lord Hanuman, usually sung right after the Hanuman Chalisa. It recalls the burning of Lanka, the Sanjeevani herb and the slaying of Ahiravan. The aarti is given below in English letters and Devanagari, with the meaning of each verse in English.",
 intro="Sing it on Tuesdays and Saturdays, after reciting the Hanuman Chalisa or the Sundarkand.",
 m=["Perform the aarti of dear Hanuman, destroyer of the wicked and the very power of Shri Ram.",
    "By his strength mountains tremble, and disease and misfortune dare not come near.",
    "The son of Anjani is mighty and always helps the saints.",
    "Shri Ram sent him with a betel-leaf token; he burned Lanka and brought back news of Sita.",
    "Lanka was a fortress with a moat as wide as the sea, yet the son of the Wind crossed it in no time.",
    "He burned Lanka, destroyed the demons and accomplished the work of Sita and Ram.",
    "When Lakshman lay unconscious, he brought the Sanjeevani herb and saved his life.",
    "He entered the underworld, broke the bonds and tore off Ahiravan's arms.",
    "With his left arm he struck down the demon army; with his right he carried the saints across.",
    "Gods, humans and sages perform his aarti, crying victory, victory, victory to Hanuman!",
    "Camphor flames glow on a golden plate as Mother Anjana performs his aarti.",
    "Whoever sings this aarti of Hanuman goes to Vaikunth and attains the highest state."],
 faqs=[("When should Hanuman aarti be done?","On Tuesdays and Saturdays, after the Hanuman Chalisa or the Sundarkand.")])

EN["lakshmi-aarti.html"] = dict(
 name="Om Jai Lakshmi Mata", sub="Lakshmi aarti, with English meaning",
 title="Om Jai Lakshmi Mata Aarti — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Om Jai Lakshmi Mata aarti lyrics in English letters and Hindi, with a simple English meaning of every verse. For Diwali Lakshmi puja, Dhanteras and Fridays.",
 answer="'Om Jai Lakshmi Mata' is the aarti of Goddess Lakshmi, sung at the Diwali Lakshmi puja, on Dhanteras and on Fridays. The aarti is given below in English letters and Devanagari, with the meaning of each verse in English.",
 intro="Sing it on Diwali night after Lakshmi puja, on Dhanteras and every Friday evening.",
 m=["Victory to you, Mother Lakshmi! Vishnu and Brahma serve you day and night.",
    "You are Uma, Rama and Brahmani — the mother of the world; the sun and moon meditate on you and the sage Narad sings your praise.",
    "You are the pure form of Durga, giver of happiness and wealth; whoever meditates on you gains prosperity, success and riches.",
    "You dwell even in the netherworld, you grant all good, you reveal the fruit of our actions and carry us across the ocean of life.",
    "In the home where you live every virtue arrives; everything becomes possible and the mind is free of worry.",
    "Without you no sacred ritual could happen and no one would have clothes; all the abundance of food and drink comes from you.",
    "You are a beautiful temple of good qualities, born from the ocean of milk; without you no one obtains the fourteen jewels.",
    "Whoever sings this aarti of Mahalakshmi is filled with joy in the heart, and their sins fall away."],
 faqs=[("When should Lakshmi aarti be done?","On Diwali night after Lakshmi puja, on Dhanteras and on Friday evenings.")])

EN["gayatri-mantra.html"] = dict(
 name="Gayatri Mantra", sub="Meaning and how to chant",
 title="Gayatri Mantra — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="The Gayatri Mantra (Om Bhur Bhuva Swaha) in English letters and Sanskrit, with its meaning in simple English and how many times to chant it.",
 answer="The Gayatri Mantra comes from the Rig Veda (3.62.10) and its seer is the sage Vishwamitra. It is a prayer to the Supreme in the form of the radiant sun (Savitr), asking that our intellect be guided in the right direction.",
 intro="Traditionally it is chanted 108 times (one mala), at sunrise or sunset; 11 or 21 times is also fine when time is short.",
 m=["We meditate on the most excellent, radiant, sin-destroying divine light of the Supreme — the source of life, remover of suffering and embodiment of bliss. May it inspire and guide our intellect on the right path."],
 faqs=[("What is the meaning of the Gayatri Mantra?","'We meditate on the radiant, purifying divine light of the Supreme; may it guide our intellect on the right path.'"),
       ("How many times should the Gayatri Mantra be chanted?","Traditionally 108 times (one mala); 11 or 21 times when time is short.")])

EN["mahamrityunjay-mantra.html"] = dict(
 name="Mahamrityunjay Mantra", sub="Meaning and 108 chants",
 title="Mahamrityunjay Mantra — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="The Mahamrityunjay Mantra (Om Tryambakam Yajamahe) in English letters and Sanskrit, with its meaning in simple English and how to chant it 108 times.",
 answer="The Mahamrityunjay Mantra is from the Rig Veda (7.59.12). It is a prayer to three-eyed Shiva for freedom from the bondage of death and for immortality, and is believed to remove illness, fear and danger.",
 intro="Chant it 108 times (one mala), ideally in the morning.",
 m=["We worship the three-eyed Lord Shiva, who is fragrant and nourishes all beings. As a ripe cucumber falls free from its vine on its own, may he free us from the bondage of death — and not from immortality (liberation)."],
 faqs=[("What does the Mahamrityunjay Mantra mean?","'We worship three-eyed Shiva. As a ripe cucumber falls free from its vine, may he free us from the bondage of death.'"),
       ("How many times should it be chanted?","One mala, that is 108 times.")])

EN["mantra-sangrah.html"] = dict(
 name="10 Essential Hindu Mantras", sub="Ganesh, Shiva, Vishnu, Durga and more",
 title="10 Essential Hindu Mantras — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Ten everyday Hindu mantras — Vakratunda Mahakaya, Om Namah Shivaya, Shantakaram, Vasudeva Sutam, Manojavam, Ya Devi Sarvabhuteshu, Saraswati Vandana and the Shanti Mantra — in English letters with meaning.",
 answer="A puja begins with the Ganesh mantra and ends with a peace (shanti) mantra. Here is one simple, widely used mantra for each major deity, with its meaning in plain English.",
 intro="Each mantra can be chanted on its own, or in this order as a short daily prayer.",
 m=["O Lord with the curved trunk and mighty body, radiant as ten million suns — always make all my work free of obstacles. (Said at the start of any task.)",
    "I bow to Shiva. Shiva's simplest and most powerful mantra, often chanted 108 times.",
    "I bow to Vishnu — peaceful in form, resting on the serpent, with a lotus at his navel, lord of the gods, support of the universe, vast as the sky, dark as a rain cloud; husband of Lakshmi, lotus-eyed, reached by yogis in meditation, who removes the fear of worldly life.",
    "I bow to Shri Krishna, son of Vasudev, destroyer of Kansa and Chanur, the supreme joy of Devaki, teacher of the world.",
    "Victory to Shri Ram — this thirteen-syllable 'taraka' mantra is the simplest way to chant Ram's name.",
    "I take refuge in the messenger of Shri Ram — swift as the mind, fast as the wind, master of the senses, foremost among the wise, son of the Wind and leader of the monkey army.",
    "To the Goddess who dwells in all beings in the form of power — salutations to her, again and again.",
    "May Goddess Saraswati protect me — white as the jasmine, the moon and snow, dressed in white, holding the veena, seated on a white lotus, ever worshipped by Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva, she who removes all dullness.",
    "Salutations to Mahalakshmi. A seed mantra chanted for wealth, happiness and prosperity.",
    "May all be happy, may all be free of illness, may all see what is good, and may no one suffer. Om peace, peace, peace."],
 faqs=[("Which mantra is said first in a puja?","The Ganesh mantra 'Vakratunda Mahakaya Suryakoti Samaprabha' — every puja and auspicious task begins with it.")])
